# Per-machine setup profile. Copy this file to .env before running
# ./bootstrap.sh or ./rebuild.sh - both refuse to run until it is set:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored, because this is a per-machine choice and never a
# repo-wide one. It is read by setup-env.sh, which turns the value below into
# the flake output bootstrap.sh/rebuild.sh build.
#
# Valid values:
#   personal - full setup: personal Homebrew formulae and GUI casks on macOS
#              (Slack, Discord, Notion, Figma, ...) alongside the shared dev
#              tooling, plus the full TeX Live scheme on every OS.
#   basic    - dev tooling only, e.g. a server: no personal formulae or casks,
#              and the minimal TeX Live scheme (just pdflatex/xelatex).
DOTFILES_SETUP=
